hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1332","Muhammad bin Ubadah Al-Wasiti narrated to us, Abu Usama narrated to us, Hisham bin Urwa narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, “that a black girl She was a slave girl from the Arabs, so they freed her, and she was with them, so one day a girl came out to them wearing a scarf of red thongs, and it fell from her. Then the kite passed by and thought he was meat, so she snatched him. They searched for him but did not find him, so they accused her of it, so they searched her until they searched before her. He said: While they were like that, the little girl passed by and dropped the scarf, and it fell among them, and she said to them: This is what you accused me of, and I am of it. She is innocent, and here he is, as you see. She came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and converted to Islam. She had a tent or tent in the mosque. Hafash, she said: She used to come to me and sit with me, and she would hardly sit with me a time without saying: The Day of the Veil is one of the wonders of our Lord. However, he was from the town of Kafr. He saved me, so I said to her: “Why don’t you sit with me unless you say this?” She said: “So you spoke to me.” Hadith: I have decreed knocking on the domes in the mosques for the purpose of seclusion, in the Book of Itikaf."
